      ],
      "source": "https://vanishinggeorgia.com/category/norman-park-ga/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Recent years have seen downtown Norman Park revitalize historic storefronts, turning them into restaurants and shops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vanishinggeorgia.com/category/norman-park-ga/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Twin Houses of Norman Park, built around 1908‑10, are a celebrated example of Queen Anne architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://vanishinggeorgia.com/category/norman-park-ga/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A granite marker commemorates Norman College’s history, with the First Baptist Church visible in the background.",
